    {
      "step_id": "tile_python_conditionals_for_loops.s01",
      "type": "explainer",
      "concept_ids": [
        "python.conditional_statements"
      ],
      "eyebrow": "Control flow",
      "title": "Branching on data: if, elif, else",
      "lede": "Make your code choose the right path based on each delivery's data.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "block_id": "tile_python_conditionals_for_loops.s01.h1",
          "text": "Branching on data: if, elif, else",
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "block_id": "tile_python_conditionals_for_loops.s01.p1",
          "text": "Not every line of code should always run — sometimes what happens next depends on the data. An if statement executes its block only when its condition is true. You can add zero or more elif parts after an if, and an optional else at the end; elif is short for 'else if' and keeps the code flat instead of deeply nested.",
          "role": "mechanism",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "python.conditional_statements"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "python.conditional_statements#f1",
              "python.conditional_statements#f2"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "python.conditional_statements#tb1",
              "python.conditional_statements#tb2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "block_id": "tile_python_conditionals_for_loops.s01.p2",
          "text": "An if/elif/else chain selects exactly one block by evaluating conditions top to bottom until one is true; if none are true, the else block (if present) runs. Each condition ends with a colon, and the block belonging to that branch is indented beneath it:\n\nif delivery_minutes < 15:\n    category = 'fast'\nelif delivery_minutes < 45:\n    category = 'normal'\nelse:\n    category = 'slow'\n\nWith delivery_minutes = 30, the first condition is false and the second is true, so category becomes 'normal' and the else branch is skipped.",
          "role": "syntax",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "python.conditional_statements"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "python.conditional_statements#f3",
              "python.conditional_statements#f4"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "python.conditional_statements#tb3",
              "python.conditional_statements#tb4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "process_flow",
          "block_id": "tile_python_conditionals_for_loops.s01.pf1",
          "title": "Which branch runs for delivery_minutes = 30?",
          "direction": "TB",
          "nodes": [
