      "title": "When does an if block run?",
      "lede": "Let's revisit the rule for when an if block executes.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "block_id": "tile_python_conditionals_for_loops.r01.h1",
          "text": "Reminder: when does an if block run?",
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "block_id": "tile_python_conditionals_for_loops.r01.p1",
          "text": "An if statement executes its block only when its condition is true — not every time the code runs. If delivery_minutes = 30 and the condition is delivery_minutes > 45, the block is skipped entirely. The block runs only when the condition evaluates to True.",
          "role": "mechanism",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "python.conditional_statements"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "python.conditional_statements#f1"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
