      ],
      "title": "Which branch runs in a chain?",
      "lede": "Let's revisit how an if/elif/else chain selects exactly one branch.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "block_id": "tile_python_conditionals_for_loops.r02.h1",
          "text": "Reminder: which branch runs in a chain?",
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "block_id": "tile_python_conditionals_for_loops.r02.p1",
          "text": "An if/elif/else chain evaluates conditions one by one from top to bottom. The first condition that is true wins — its block runs and all others are skipped. If no condition is true, the else block (if present) runs. With delivery_minutes = 30: the first condition (< 15) is false, the second (< 45) is true, so category = 'normal' runs and the else branch is skipped.",
          "role": "mechanism",
          "lineage": {
